    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1165">

                <pb facs="1280" n="1270" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg1270"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.62114/12–1044: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Political Adviser on the Staff of the
                        Supreme Allied Commander, Mediterranean Theater</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caserta</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-10T13:00:00+01:00">December 10,
                            1944—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1669. Re my 411, September 16. British military authorities are assuming that our
                    policy is same as theirs in providing for repatriation <pb facs="1281" n="1271"
                        xml:id="pg1271"/> of Soviet citizens now or in future held as POWs<anchor
                        n="89" xml:id="d1165-f1"/> irrespective of whether individuals concerned
                    desire to return to Soviet Union. Inasmuch as not inconsiderable numbers of
                    Soviet POWs are acquired by American forces in this theater and handed over to
                    British for disposition we would appreciate early information as to whether
                    United States Government does in fact subscribe to British policy in this
                    connection.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1165-f1" n="89" xml:id="d1165-f1-content">
                <p>Prisoners of war.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
